    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Product 2378\" is a compilation album released in 1990 by the UK label Telstar, known primarily for mainstream and telemarketed compilations. The album features a mix of Electronic and Rock genres, capturing a snapshot of the indie and alternative music scene of the time. Its release was notable because Telstar, often viewed as a \"soulless and mainstream\" major label, ventured into indie compilations, which caused some surprise among music fans and critics.\n\nMusically, \"Product 2378\" blends electronic textures with rock elements, reflecting the transitional period in late 1980s and early 1990s music when genres were increasingly hybridized. As a various artists compilation, it does not belong to a single artist's discography but rather serves as a curated collection that highlights emerging trends and sounds within the indie and electronic rock scenes. While it did not achieve significant commercial acclaim or lasting mainstream impact, the album holds a place as an interesting artifact from Telstar’s broader strategy to diversify beyond its usual compilation fare.",
